   "claims": [
    "(Note that you can also treat this $1,000 as the initial value of your loan with simple interest).",
    "To get a monthly interest, divide this value by the number of months in a year (12).",
    "An example of simple interest in practice You inherit $1,000,000 and intend to use it to provide a steady income - you don't want to spend it, nor invest it.",
    "You put it into a bank account with a 5% annual interest rate.",
    "The real-life examples of simple interest loans Well, not everyone will inherit $1,000,000 (although we sincerely wish you that).",
    "So: $5,000 + $150 = $5,150 Assume that you have a credit card with a $2,500 limit and a 15% interest rate that is not compounded.",
    "The interest that will accrue on your credit card this month is: $1,700 × 15% / 12 = $21.25 However, be aware that credit cards usually have compounded interest rate.",
    "We also need to assume that, the interest rate is 4% and is constant over time.",
    "To find the future value, F, of simple interest, follow these steps: Write down the simple interest value, r, as a decimal (e.g., 5% is 0.05).",
    "6% interest on a $30,000 loan is $1,800 per year or $150 per month."
